      <div class="prose-content text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary" data-aos="fade-up"><h2 id="sec-1">Quick Overview</h2><p>Precision electric kettles have transformed home coffee and tea preparation. Whether brewing delicate green tea at 175°F or extracting the perfect pour-over at 205°F, the right kettle makes a measurable difference. We tested 12 temperature-controlled kettles for accuracy, speed, build quality, and usability.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Product</th><th>Price</th><th>Rating</th><th>Capacity</th><th>Temp Range</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td><strong>Fellow Stagg EKG</strong></td><td>$165</td><td>⭐ 4.9/5</td><td>0.9L</td><td>176-212°F</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><strong>Breville Vari Control</strong></td><td>$130</td><td>⭐ 4.7/5</td><td>1.2L</td><td>160-212°F</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><strong>Cuisinart CPK-15</strong></td><td>$69.99</td><td>⭐ 4.5/5</td><td>1.5L</td><td>160-212°F</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><strong>BONAVITA 1.0L</strong></td><td>$79.99</td><td>⭐ 4.6/5</td><td>1.0L</td><td>185-212°F</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><strong>Smeg Variable Temp</strong></td><td>$149</td><td>⭐ 4.4/5</td><td>1.7L</td><td>167-212°F</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><strong>KitchenAid KEK1224</strong></td><td>$99.99</td><td>⭐ 4.3/5</td><td>1.25L</td><td>160-212°F</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><strong>OXO Brew Barista</strong></td><td>$99.99</td><td>⭐ 4.5/5</td><td>1.0L</td><td>190-212°F</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><strong>Jacobsen Salt Craft</strong></td><td>$120</td><td>⭐ 4.4/5</td><td>1.25L</td><td>Pre-set modes</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><strong>T-fal Express Ion</strong></td><td>$44.99</td><td>⭐ 4.1/5</td><td>1.7L</td><td>3 presets</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><strong>Hamilton Beach Programmable</strong></td><td>$34.99</td><td>⭐ 4.0/5</td><td>1.7L</td><td>3 presets</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="sec-2">How We Tested</h2><p>Each kettle underwent rigorous testing with calibrated thermometers to verify temperature accuracy within ±2°F of the set point. We also measured boil time, temperature hold over 30 minutes, flow control precision for pour-over, noise level, build quality, and interface intuitiveness.</p><h2 id="sec-3">Top Picks Reviewed</h2><h3>1. Fellow Stagg EKG — Best Overall</h3><p>The Fellow Stagg EKG is the quintessential precision kettle for coffee and tea enthusiasts. Variable temperature control spans 176-212°F in 1-degree increments. The built-in stopwatch and flow-restrictor gooseneck spout make it ideal for pour-over. Temperature accuracy was within ±1°F across all tested settings.</p><div style="background:#F7F4EF;border-left:3px solid #C9A962;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:1.5rem 0;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-size:0.95rem"><strong>Best for:</strong> Pour-over coffee enthusiasts, tea connoisseurs, and anyone who values design alongside performance.</p></div><h3>2. Breville Vari Control — Best Large Capacity</h3><p>At 1.2L, the Breville offers generous capacity with precise control from 160-212°F. The soft-opening lid prevents splashing, and the digital display clearly shows set and current temperatures. Stay-cool handle and auto-shutoff provide safety and convenience.</p><h3>3. BONAVITA 1.0L — Best for Coffee</h3><p>The BONAVITA pre-infusion mode mimics hand-pouring by briefly saturating grounds before the main brew cycle. Its 1500W heating element brings water to temperature quickly. The ON/OFF switch with indicator light is simple and effective.</p><h2 id="sec-4">Temperature Guide</h2><ul><li><strong>Green tea:</strong> 160-180°F</li><li><strong>White tea:</strong> 175-185°F</li><li><strong>Oolong tea:</strong> 185-200°F</li><li><strong>Black tea:</strong> 200-212°F</li><li><strong>Pour-over coffee:</strong> 195-205°F</li><li><strong>French press:</strong> 200-205°F</li></ul><h2 id="sec-5">FAQs</h2><h3>Why does water temperature matter?</h3><p>Water temperature directly affects extraction. Too hot over-extracts bitter compounds; too cool under-extracts sour, weak flavor. Precision ensures optimal extraction for each beverage type.</p><h3>Do I need a gooseneck kettle?</h3><p>For pour-over coffee, yes — controlled flow rate is essential. For tea, a standard spout suffices. The Fellow Stagg EKG serves both purposes elegantly.</p><h2 id="sec-6">Final Verdict</h2><div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1A1A1A 0%,#2A2A2A 100%);color:white;padding:2rem;border-radius:12px;margin-top:2rem"><p style="font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 0.75rem 0;color:#C9A962">Our Recommendation</p><p style="margin:0;line-height:1.8">The <strong>Fellow Stagg EKG</strong> at $165 is the best precision kettle. For larger households, the <strong>Breville Vari Control</strong> at $130 offers more capacity. Budget buyers should consider the <strong>Cuisinart CPK-15</strong> at $70.</p></div></div>
